{"slug": "am-armee-terre-cuite", "fichier": "Xian, Terracotta Army (6170329474).jpg", "largeur": 640, "hauteur": 424, "data": "data:image/webp;base64,", "auteur": "Arian Zwegers from Brussels, Belgium", "licence": "CC BY 2.0", "licence_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0", "description": "The Terracotta Army or the \"Terra Cotta Warriors and Horses\", is a collection of terracotta sculptures depicting the armies of Qin Shi Huang, the first Emperor of China. It is a form of funerary art buried with the emperor in 210–209 BC and whose purpose was to protect the emperor in his afterlife. ", "source": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File%3AXian%2C%20Terracotta%20Army%20%286170329474%29.jpg"}